-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Grid Size:** The extrapolation formula requires at least 3 voxels in each dimension to access $V_{n-2}$ and $V_{n-3}$ (or equivalent indices). If the grid is smaller than 3 voxels in any dimension, the method fails.
-- **Boundary Continuity:** The choice of extrapolation affects gradient continuity at edges. The 4th-order extrapolation ensures smoothness but assumes the SDF is well-behaved near the boundary [G].
+**Edge Cases:**
+- **Grid Dimensions:** The extrapolation formula requires at least 3 voxels in each dimension ($N \ge 3$) to access indices $n, n-1, n-2$ and $1, 0, 2$. If $N < 3$, the method is undefined or requires fallback to lower-order schemes [G].
+- **Boundary Continuity:** While the extrapolation ensures 4th-order accuracy at the immediate boundary, the transition from interior to boundary gradients may exhibit discontinuities if the field is not smooth [G].
